    console.log(JSON.stringify({
      method: req.method,
      path: req.originalUrl,
      status: res.statusCode,
      ms: Number(process.hrtime.bigint() - start) / 1e6,
      userId: req.user && req.user.id,
      accountId: req.user && req.user.accountId,
    }));
  });
  next();
});
```

- **Placement:** registering it before `sessionUser` means rejected 401 requests are logged too. `req.user` is read when the response finishes, by which time `sessionUser` has set it.
